infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Static vs dynamic compression: where you pay the cost
  desc Precompress immutable assets once; compress per-user HTML on the fly — match the method to the asset
  compares
    - label Static compression
      children
        - label Compress once at build time
          desc Precompressed file served directly with Content-Encoding: br
        - label Request-time cost — 0 ms
          desc No CPU per request; the compressed file already exists
        - label Best for immutable assets — JS, CSS
          desc Same bytes for every user, so compress the hardest
        - label Senior pattern — static brotli everywhere it can
          desc Brotli's 70-90% reduction at zero per-request cost
    - label Dynamic compression
      children
        - label Compress on the fly, per request
          desc Recomputed for every response the server emits
        - label Request-time cost — brotli 5-30 ms, gzip 1-5 ms
          desc CPU paid on every single request
        - label Best for per-user HTML
          desc Body varies per request, so it cannot be precompressed
        - label Senior pattern — dynamic gzip for HTML
          desc Cheaper 1-5 ms encode beats brotli's 5-30 ms here
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f59e0b
